{"id":17866,"name":"Etowah County","slug":"etowah-county","state":"Alabama","code":"AL","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien/tax-lien-states/alabama-tax-lien-sales-how-to-get-12-interest/etowah-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-13T12:29:23","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Lien Sale","bidProcedure":"Bid down the interest rate","redemptionPeriod":"3 years","interestRate":"Up to 12%","extra":[{"label":"Typical Date of Sale","value":"Annually, typically around April or May"},{"label":"Sale Contact","value":"Revenue Commissioner – Etowah County"},{"label":"Auction Site","value":"GovEase.com"},{"label":"County Website","value":"Etowah County"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed aligncenter is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"rbTYZzFzn1PwvGgpOkjxAV2v06qRdJMNduhmSxc9HUeoQBHbu4wZJmPi5EWQ8j3lhGltCULWtF3oycfp5S6942OfDiByI17Xa70\"><iframe title=\"Claim Your 12% Yearly Return! - Etowah County - Alabama Tax Lien Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/iFdN2YJJLt4?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Claim-Your-12%-Yearly-Return!---Etowah-County,-Alabama-Tax-Lien-Investing\">Claim Your 12% Yearly Return! &#8211; Etowah County, Alabama Tax Lien Investing</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Investing in tax lien sales in Etowah County, Alabama, offers a fantastic opportunity for potential returns of up to 12%. This process allows you to invest in tax liens, earn interest, and potentially acquire property if the lien is not redeemed. The entire process is streamlined and conducted online via <a href=\"http://govease.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">GovEase</mark></a>, making it easy to get started without entry fees.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Understanding-Tax-Lien-Certificates\">Understanding Tax Lien Certificates</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Tax Lien Certificates:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>When you purchase a tax lien certificate, you pay the outstanding property taxes on a property.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The property owner then owes you the unpaid taxes plus interest, capped at 12% annually in Alabama.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>If the property owner fails to redeem the lien within three years, you could foreclose and potentially own the property.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Example Investment:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>If you buy a tax lien for $1,000 with a 12% interest rate, you could earn $120 per year.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Over three years, your total potential earnings would be $360 if the lien is not redeemed sooner.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Steps-to-Start-Tax-Lien-Investing\">Steps to Start Tax Lien Investing</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Research and Understand Local Laws:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>It&#8217;s crucial to know the legal framework in Etowah County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Redemption period is three years before you can foreclose on the property.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Visit the Local Treasurer&#8217;s Website:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://etowahcounty.org/delinquent-real-property-for-2022/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Etowah County Delinquent Real Property</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://etowahcounty.org/department/revenue-commission/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Etowah County Revenue Commission</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Check the Auction Site:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://govease.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">GovEase Auction Site</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Read the Details About Tax Liens:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Understand the sale schedule and essential details provided on the auction site.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Contact the County Office:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For further inquiries, you can contact the Revenue Commissioner of Etowah County at (256) 549-1444.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Important-Details\">Important Details</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Etowah-County-Courthouse.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Etowah-County-Courthouse-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Etowah-County-Courthouse-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Etowah-C